    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205683": {
      "title": "Center Director - Delhi Campus Child Care Center",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Center Director - Delhi Campus Child Care Center SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Center Director - Delhi Campus Child Care Center Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Center Director - Delhi Campus Child Care Center Category: Delhi Campus Child Care Center, Inc. (DC4) Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Delhi Campus Child Care Center Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Oct 9, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: n/a Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $63,000.00 - $63,000.00 Position ID: 205683 Share About SUNY Delhi: Delhi Campus Child Care Center, Inc. (DC4) is a not-for-profit corporation licensed by the New York State Office of Children and Family Services (OCFS) and participates in QUALITYstarsNY. DC4 was established in 1985 to serve the childcare needs of SUNY students, faculty and staff of SUNY Delhi (CADI, DC4, Research Foundation, or anyone who works on campus), and New York State employees. Enrollment is also open to the community. A Board of Directors representing these constituencies governs the Center. DC4 is located at 1104 Arbor Hill Road on lower campus just past the SUNY Delhi College Farm and Decker Auto lab. The state-of-the-art facility includes: 5 classrooms, 4 large playgrounds, kitchen, large indoor gym and library, and family resource area. DC4 is licensed to serve 85 children ages 6 weeks - 12 years. Delhi Campus Child Care Center, Inc. is in partnership with DelArc's Carousel Children's Services (CCS). Carousel Children's Services program provides a variety of individualized services to children, birth to age 5. Special education teachers and therapists work individually with each child and their family. Children enrolled through CCS attend DC4 during the Delaware Academy Central School District at Delhi calendar year, plus a 6-week summer program. Up to twenty-four children enrolled through CCS are integrated into the two preschool programs. DC4 and CCS staff work collaboratively to develop a program that ensures the needs of all children are met. Job Description: Reporting to the Board of Directors, the Center Director is responsible for the overall day-to-day operation and administration of the Center and for creating a safe environment, which is warm and loving, and contributes to the emotional, physical, educational, and social development of the children in the Center. In accordance with the licensing regulations set for the Center by the OCFS, specific duties and responsibilities include: Leads day-to-day administrative operations with strong strategic oversight, ensuring  institutional policies and governance directives established by the Board of Directors are effectively executed. Oversees comprehensive staff supervision and professional development, managing the complete personnel lifecycle from recruitment, onboarding, and training to performance evaluation, coaching, and retention. Maintains high-standard, comprehensive programming by overseeing curriculum design, classroom instruction, health and social services, and active family education initiatives. Directs financial and administrative systems to maximize resource efficiency. Monitors operating budgets, spearheads grant development, administers contracts, and ensures robust internal controls to safeguard the Center's financial health. Acts as the primary public advocate for the Center, cultivating external networks, building community partnerships, and advancing its mission within the broader region. Maintains transparent, collaborative communication with the Board of Directors by attending all meetings and committee sessions, and delivering timely, comprehensive institutional reports. Sustains a strong, cooperative relationship with SUNY Delhi, ensuring the Center operates as a valuable, integrated asset to the college community. Collaborates closely with the Director of Carousel Children's Services to align program delivery, meet the diverse needs of enrolled children, and promote staff harmony. Partners with appropriate regulatory and funding agencies to maintain full program licensure, accreditation, and adherence to operational standards. Uphold state and institutional safety guidelines by maintaining required staff-to-student ratios through active classroom coverage during staffing gaps. Requirements: Bachelor's degree, including or in addition to 12 credits in Early Childhood, Child Development or a related field; one year of full-time teaching experience in a child care center, family or group family day care home or other early childhood program; and one year of experience in supervising staff in a child care program or related field work; OR a New York State Children's Program Administrator Credential; one year of full-time teaching experience in a child care center, family or group family day care home or other early childhood program; and one year of experience in supervising staff in a child care program or a related field of work; OR an Associate's degree in Early Childhood or related field, with a plan of study leading to a Bachelor's degree or a New York State Children's Program Administrator Credential; two years of full-time teaching experience in a child care center, family or group family day care home or other early childhood program; and two years of experience supervising staff in a child care program or a related field of work; OR Child Development Associate Credential or other office-recognized credential, with a plan of study leading to a Bachelor's degree or a New York State Children's Program Administrator Credential; two years of full-time teaching experience in a child care center, family or group family day care home or other early childhood program; and two years of experience supervising staff in a child care program or a related field of work. Preferred Qualifications (in addition to at least one of the above minimum requirements): Demonstrated background in executive-level administration, business operations, and/or accounting management. Working knowledge of QuickBooks for operational accounting, ledger management, and financial reporting. Comprehensive understanding of New York State Office of Children and Family Services (NYSOCFS) child care center regulations and compliance standards. Hands-on experience managing payroll, CACFP/nutrition programs, facility work orders, block grants, and institutional supply procurement. Additional Information: Salary Starting at: $63,000 Work Schedule: Monday through Friday days, occasional evenings and weekends This position offers benefits: Retirement Life Insurance Paid vacation and sick time Paid holiday break: between Christmas day and New Year's Day Child care assistance Disability insurance and long term disability insurance Education assistance DC4 is committed to providing a safe and productive learning environment for all children, staff, and visitors. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the full background check series and verification of credentials presented. The Center Director is a DC4 employee. This is not a SUNY Delhi/NYS position. Application Instructions: To apply, please submit: Letter of interest Transcripts from any/all previous institution(s) Resume Contact information for at least three professional references This posting will remain open until filled. Delhi Child Care Center is an AA/EOE employer Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205593": {
      "title": "FACULTY: Mechatronics Design",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: FACULTY:  Mechatronics Design SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: FACULTY:  Mechatronics Design Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details FACULTY:  Mechatronics Design Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Applied Technology and Architecture Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Oct 8, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 356430 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $50,906.00 - $50,906.00 Position ID: 205593 Share About SUNY Delhi: Fast Facts About SUNY Delhi Job Description: SUNY Delhi seeks a dynamic, forward-thinking, and engaging full-time tenure-track faculty member for the Mechatronics Design (two-year AOS & AAS track) , and Mechatronics Technology (BT) Programs . Desirable candidates will have the ability to handle the responsibilities of but are not limited to implementation of industry standards in curriculum coursework (ANSI, ASME, NEMA, ISO, IEC, etc.). The successful candidate will have the ability to teach a variety of introductory and upper-level courses in the mechanical design realm, focusing primarily on mechanical drafting, 3D modeling, 3D simulation, and mechanical assemblies, based on a thorough knowledge of 2D and 3D parametric design and simulation, industry standards and practices (ASME Y14.5, etc.), and relevant industrial experience. Special consideration will also be given to those candidates with additional skills related to automated production and process control systems, PLC system design, programming, and troubleshooting, and associated electrical design and construction standards (NFPA 70 2014, NFPA 70e, NFPA 79. or newer, etc.). Faculty members in our Mechatronics program are responsible for the following: Program Development Participate in annual systematic assessment of the program Participate in analyzing data and recommending curriculum and programmatic revisions where necessary Teaching Responsibilities Provide evidence-based instruction following the policies set forth by the College Provide hands-on, lab-based instruction on various construction methods, including job site safety and safe operation of tools and equipment Post and keep regular office hours for the convenience of students Participate in the assessment of course, student learning, and program outcomes Incorporate student service-learning opportunities Advisement Assist in advisement of students Guide and counsel students toward personal and career development Track student's completion of progression requirements Academic & Organization Commitment Serve on campus committees Mentoring Adjunct Faculty Participate in full and part-time faculty meetings Participate in accreditation reviews and reports Engage in the academic and organizational life of the college Pursue scholarly interests Requirements: A minimum of an Associates Degree in a related field and 5 years of relevant experience plus demonstrated teaching/training ability. Preferred Qualifications: A Bachelor's Degree with at least 3 years of relevant experience including prior teaching experience or Bachelor's Degree with at least 5 years of relevant experience. Additional Information: Start Date: Spring 2027 semester Annual Salary $50,906 This is a full-time, tenure track position with an annual 10-month obligation This position offers full New York State benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. This position offers full New York State UUP (FT ) benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country with an excellent fringe benefits package More Information for Prospective Employees Clery Statement Applicants interested in positions may access the Annual Security Report (ASR ) for SUNY Delhi online. The ASR contains information on campus security policies and certain campus crime statistics. Crime statistics are reported in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Applicants may request a hard copy of the ASR by contacting the SUNY Delhi University Police Department at 607-746-4700. Application Instructions: To apply, please submit: Letter of interest Resume Contact information for three professional references For full consideration please apply by October 30th, 2026 Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205423": {
      "title": "FACULTY: Refrigeration",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: FACULTY: Refrigeration SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: FACULTY: Refrigeration Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details FACULTY: Refrigeration Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Applied Technology and Architecture Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Oct 8, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $50,906.00 - $50,906.00 Position ID: 205423 Share About SUNY Delhi: Fast Facts about SUNY Delhi Job Description: SUNY Delhi prides itself on being a welcoming college community for all. Diversity, equity, and inclusiveness are integral components of the highest-quality academic programs and the strongest campus climate. The college seeks a wide range of applicants for its positions so that inclusive excellence will be affirmed. SUNY Delhi seeks a dynamic, forward-thinking, and engaging faculty member to join the School of Applied Technologies starting in January for the Spring 2027 semester. Applications are being accepted for a full-time, 10-month, tenure-track faculty member in the School of Applied Technologies and Architecture , teaching Refrigeration and Air Conditioning courses. The successful candidate will have a good working knowledge of both domestic and commercial refrigeration and air conditioning systems. This should include a strong knowledge of electrical systems and controls used throughout the industry. Faculty members in our HVAC program are responsible for the following: Program Development Participate in annual systematic assessment of the program Participate in analyzing data and recommending curriculum and programmatic revisions where necessary Teaching Responsibilities Provide evidence-based instruction following the policies set forth by the College Provide hands-on, lab-based instruction on various construction methods, including job site safety and safe operation of tools and equipment Post and keep regular office hours for the convenience of students Participate in the assessment of course, student learning, and program outcomes Incorporate student service-learning opportunities Advisement Assist in advisement of students Guide and counsel students toward personal and career development Track student's completion of progression requirements Academic & Organization Commitment Serve on campus committees Mentoring Adjunct Faculty Participate in full and part-time faculty meetings Participate in accreditation reviews and reports Engage in the academic and organizational life of the college Pursue scholarly interests Requirements: Associate's degree in a related field and 3 years of professional experience in a related field OR High School Diploma and 10 years in a related field (would require the applicant to attain an Associate Degree within 6 years) EPA 608 Certification NYS Driver's license with an acceptable driving record Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a related field with three years of professional experience in a related field Seven or more years of professional experience in a related field Experience in teaching or working with young adults Demonstrated ability to teach diverse populations Understanding the value of civic engagement Additional Information: Salary: $50,906 This is a 10-month academic year, tenure track position This position offers full New York State UUP (FT) benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country. Click here for more Information for Prospective Employees SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. Application Instructions: SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character and global citizenship. To apply please attach the following items and provide a short statement in your cover letter on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. Cover letter Resume Contact information for three professional references For full consideration please apply by November 8, 2026 and will remain posted until filled. Clery Statement Applicants interested in positions may access the Annual Security Report (ASR) for SUNY Delhi online. The ASR contains information on campus security policies and certain campus crime statistics. Crime statistics are reported in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Applicants may request a hard copy of the ASR by contacting the SUNY Delhi University Police Department at 607-746-4700. SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer. SUNY Delhi does not discriminate. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Your application will not be accepted if you require sponsorship to work in the United States. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205657": {
      "title": "Senior Counselor",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Senior Counselor SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Senior Counselor Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Senior Counselor Category: Staff - UUP Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Health & Counseling Services Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Oct 9, 2026 Closes: Nov 9, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 356449 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $63,000.00 - $68,000.00 Position ID: 205657 Share About SUNY Delhi: Fast Facts About SUNY Delhi Job Description: Serves as a lead counselor in the design and implementation of mental health programs for the campus community including the provision of individual and group counseling to students, assessment, referrals, and consultation with faculty and staff around issues related to the developmental and psychological needs of college students. Collaborates with the Director of Health Services to provide direction to staff in the absence of the Director of Counseling Services. Provides services using developmentally appropriate, culturally responsive, and student-centered practices that recognize the range of backgrounds, experiences, perspectives, abilities, identities, and needs represented within the campus community. The Senior Counselor is expected to provide regular evening and weekend presence in the Residence Halls, including working one evening each week and one to two weekend days per month. Specific days and schedules will be determined in coordination with the incumbent, the needs of the Residence Halls, and the overall responsibilities of the position. Provides assessment, individual counseling, group counseling, and case management services to students seeking assistance for a wide range of mental health concerns, including personal, social, educational, and vocational concerns. Uses developmentally appropriate and culturally responsive practices and considers relevant aspects of each student's background, lived experience, values, abilities, family and community context, and circumstances in assessment, treatment planning, intervention, and referral, while applying consistent professional and clinical standards. This may include being assigned more complex and difficult cases. Performs crisis intervention and consults or refers to psychiatric and/or medical resources as needed. Demonstrates the ability to assess and respond to crisis while recognizing that culture, disability, communication differences, previous experiences with institutions or systems, and other individual circumstances may affect how distress presents and how students seek or receive assistance. Assists with departmental response to mental health related emergencies involving students. Develops and facilitates training and educational programs with staff, faculty, and/or students that promote interpersonal skills, academic success, well-being, help-seeking, healthy relationships, and effective communication across differences. Recommends and designs educational programs to assist students in their development. Programs should reflect an understanding of the varied experiences, circumstances, and barriers that may influence student development, belonging, well-being, and access to support. Provides consultation and resources to faculty, staff, administrators, students, and families regarding the developmental and mental health needs of college students, including factors that may affect students' access to, comfort with, or use of counseling and other support services. Assists with development and facilitation of initial and on-going training of residence hall and other appropriate staff. Training may include recognizing and responding effectively to differences in communication, behavior, help-seeking, disability, cultural experience, and other factors that may affect student interactions and well-being. Supports specialized programs and services responsive to identified student and campus needs, as assigned by the Director of Counseling Services Assists in processing student withdrawals, leaves of absence, and re-admissions as directed. Assists in the development and implementation of department/unit policies and procedures. Assist with onboarding and clinical supervision of new clinical staff as appropriate. Researches relevant and emerging college mental health and student-development issues and uses evidence-informed practices to support departmental programming and services. Participates in enrollment and retention initiatives such as open houses, orientation, and other events. Participates in assessment efforts of the Counseling Center. including assessment of service utilization, barriers to access, student needs, program effectiveness, and opportunities to improve student engagement and outcomes. Requirements: Master's degree in Counseling, Social Work or closely related field. NYS licensed or license eligible to practice mental health counseling. (LCSW, LMHC, LMSW, Licensed Psychologist). One (1) year of clinical experience. Generalist clinical skills and experience in assessing and intervening with a range of disorders, concerns, and degrees of pathology in treatment. Demonstrated cultural responsiveness and ability to provide effective counseling services to students with a wide range of backgrounds, identities, lived experiences, beliefs, abilities, and perspectives. Demonstrated ability to establish therapeutic relationships characterized by respect, curiosity, trust, and effective communication with students whose experiences, perspectives, values, or identities may differ from the counselor's own. Awareness, knowledge of and skills to provide services to members of marginalized populations. Commitment to a developmental philosophy toward clients and a proactive student development perspective involving an active relationship with the campus community. Ability to handle a busy caseload in a dynamic environment. Ability to handle spontaneous work demands while undertaking projects that require advance planning. Outstanding interpersonal, oral and written communication skills and ability to work effectively and cooperatively with a team of professionals. Ability to maintain up to date and accurate documentation. Preferred Qualifications: Experience providing counseling, outreach, education, or consultation to college students representing a broad range of backgrounds, abilities, experiences, and perspectives. Experience in crisis intervention. Experience with electronic medical records. Experience giving presentations, and leading group discussions. Experience providing training and education to students, faculty and staff. Additional Information: Starting date: ASAP Work schedule: Calendar year,11-month position with a non-obligation period in June or July, to be determined in consultation with the hiring manager. Salary: $63,000-$68,000 Reports to: Director of Counseling Services Budget Title:  Senior Counselor, SL-4 This position offers full New York State UUP (FT) benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country with an excellent fringe benefits package Click here for more Information for Prospective Employees SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. If you need a disability-related accommodation, please contact ehretsrh@delhi.edu Clery Statement Applicants interested in positions may access the Annual Security Report (ASR) for SUNY Delhi online. The ASR contains information on campus security policies and certain campus crime statistics. Crime statistics are reported in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Applicants may request a hard copy of the ASR by contacting the SUNY Delhi University Police Department at 607-746-4700. Application Instructions: To apply, please submit: Letter of interest Resume or Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three professional references Optional statement requested: SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity, and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character, and global citizenship. Please provide a short statement on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. For full consideration, please apply by November 9, 2026. Position will remain open until filled. SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer. SUNY Delhi does not discriminate. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Your application will not be accepted if you require sponsorship to work in the United States. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203589": {
      "title": "Farrell Team Tech Crew (Fall 2026)",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Farrell Team Tech Crew (Fall 2026) SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Farrell Team Tech Crew (Fall 2026) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Farrell Team Tech Crew (Fall 2026) Category: Active Student Jobs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Farrell Student and Community Center and Campus Events Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Aug 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Hourly Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $16.00 - $16.00 Position ID: 203589 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi, founded in 1913, is a student-centered college that offers specialized certificates, nationally-recognized associate degree programs, unique baccalaureate degrees and a master's degree in Nursing Education. A targeted expansion of baccalaureate programs through satellite campuses and on-line has led to a record enrollment of more than 3,400 students. A charter member of the State University of New York system, the college is also recognized for forming innovative partnerships that enhance regional economic growth, and for the college's commitment to civic engagement, applied learning, and service-learning. Located in the beautiful foothills of the Catskill Mountains, Delhi and the surrounding area offer outstanding recreational opportunities and small-town charm. Binghamton, the Capitol District and Metropolitan New York are easily accessible. SUNY Delhi was recognized in 2009, 2010 and 2015 as a \"Great College to Work for\" by the Chronicle of Higher Education. Job Description: The Farrell Student & Community Center is looking for students to serve as a member of the Farrell Team Tech Crew.  Reporting to the Director of the Farrell Student & Community Center and Campus Events, members of the Farrell Team Tech Crew largely assist in late night and weekend programming associated with the CSLE Department and Student Senate-funded club and organization events in their audio-visual needs for event held in and near the Farrell Student and Community Center.  Students in the position would work independently or in small groups to work with the program sponsors to ensure events Job duties include, but are not limited to: Provide general A/V technology support for CSLE and/or Student Senate-funded student campus events in the Farrell Student & Community Center. Keep the A/V storage areas and The Okun Theatre Tech Desk and Projection Booth neat and organized Assist in maintaining an updated inventory of supplies Notify the Director of any equipment or repair needs Attend required student employee staff meetings and trainings Other duties as assigned by the Director. Requirements: Applicants must: Have a minimum of a 2.25 GPA Have a clean campus judicial record Be able to work with others in a team Have good verbal and written communication skills Be good problem-solvers and troubleshooters Be available nights and weekends (schedules are varied and hours are sporadic depending on events scheduled and the needs of the sponsors.) Carry a minimum of 12 institutional credits at SUNY Delhi Show proficiency in and/or willingness to learn basic theatre tech equipment. Desired Qualifications: Prior experience with high school theaters or similar.  Proficiency in basic sound reinforcement, microphones, audio cabling, theatre lighting design and usage.  Familiarity with basic video equipment hook ups and computers. Additional Information: This position works in conjunction with the Farrell Building Team Members who work the Information Desk and the Farrell Game Room.  Student Team members will be asked to participate in training sessions throughout the semester.  Farrell Team Tech Crew members can expect, on average, 1-2 hours a week minimum, but can be as much as 6-8 hours per week depending on the events needing coverage,  Hours are mostly night and can include weekends. Application Instructions: Please upload your Co-Curricular Transcript or Resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202432": {
      "title": "Swimming Instructors (Fall 2026)",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Swimming Instructors (Fall 2026) SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Swimming Instructors (Fall 2026) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Swimming Instructors (Fall 2026) Category: Active Student Jobs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Jul 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Hourly Ref. No.: RTF # 350920 Position ID: 202432 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi, founded in 1913, is a student-centered college that offers specialized certificates, nationally-recognized associate degree programs, unique baccalaureate degrees and a master's degree in Nursing Education. A targeted expansion of baccalaureate programs through satellite campuses and on-line has led to a record enrollment of more than 3,400 students. A charter member of the State University of New York system, the college is also recognized for forming innovative partnerships that enhance regional economic growth, and for the college's commitment to civic engagement, applied learning, and service-learning. Located in the beautiful foothills of the Catskill Mountains, Delhi and the surrounding area offer outstanding recreational opportunities and small-town charm. Binghamton, the Capitol District and Metropolitan New York are easily accessible. SUNY Delhi was recognized in 2009, 2010 and 2015 as a \"Great College to Work for\" by the Chronicle of Higher Education. Job Description: Responsible for planning and teaching group swim lessons and private lessons and Water Safety Thorough knowledge and application of swimming and water safety skills Thorough knowledge and application of teaching swimming and water safety skills An understanding of facility characteristics, rules, policies and procedures Leadership and public relations skills Communication skills Decision-making skills Adapt your teaching approaches to the age, experience and ability of participants so they can meet course objectives Communicate regularly with participants to ensure they are aware of progress Complete records and reports in a timely manner and return then to lesson coordinator Participate in regular in-service training sessions Complete additional duties as assigned by supervisor RESPONSIBLE TO: Swim Lesson Coordinator, Aquatics Director Plans and organizes personal class teaching outlines, methods and goals that support the general teaching outlines provided by the Aquatics Manager *-- Organizes and directs activities of assigned students in order to provide a high level of quality instruction for all students. *-- Insures that all class students are registered, with a registration card prior to beginning class, are thoroughly involved, are on a first-name personalized basis in meaningful instruction for the two-week duration and are in receipt of appropriate certificates and awards as the session concludes. Show up 10 minutes before you start your first class to set up. Enforces pool safety standards and facility operational rules for all individuals using the facilities. Completes and submits records and documentation of completed lessons to the Aquatics Manager Requirements: -- Must be at least 16 years of age. -- Must be a high school graduate or currently attending high school. Necessary Knowledge, Skills and Abilities -- Outstanding aquatic skills and proficiency. -- Ability to demonstrate a pleasing personality and positive/assertive character traits. -- Ability to communicate effectively with children and adults. -- Ability to remain alert, attentive, and responsible. Additional Information: Wages: $16.80/hour Application Instructions: Please review the SUNY Child Protection Policy and complete the Policy Acknowledgment form to be uploaded along with resume: Child Protection Policy: https://www.suny.edu/sunypp/documents.cfm?doc_id=762 Policy Acknowledgment: https://www.delhi.edu/mydelhi/faculty-staff/administration/human_resources/pdf/Child Protection Policy Acknowledgement Form.pdf Fill out an Application.  (Be sure to save it to your computer using \"save as\") Upload your application, resume AND policy acknowledgement form when prompted **Please be sure your Adobe Acrobat software is up to date and that you are opening the application in Internet Explorer. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
