    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=201006": {
      "title": "Help Desk Assistant (Fall 2026)",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Help Desk Assistant (Fall 2026) SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Help Desk Assistant (Fall 2026) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Help Desk Assistant (Fall 2026) Category: Active Student Jobs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: CIS Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: May 29, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Ref. No.: RTF #350880 Position ID: 201006 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi has been delivering student-centered education in the foothills of the scenic Catskill Mountains for more than 100 years. A member of the State University of New York system, SUNY Delhi offers a supportive environment, and the chance to work among energetic colleagues and students on a friendly and inclusive campus. Job Description: Help Desk Assistants will be expected to carry themselves in a professional, polite manner when interacting with Help Desk users.  Assistants must be able to follow written and oral directions from CIS supervisory staff and our Help Desk ticketing system.   Typical duties include but are not limited to: answering phones, using our Help Desk software to create and assign tickets, moving hardware (i.e.: computers, phones, etc.), and assist wherever needed within the CIS department.  We are looking for students who can both work independently and as a member of a team. Responsibilities: Answer Help Desk phones to provide first-level contact and problem resolution for all users with hardware, software and applications problems. Initiate and maintain detailed tickets within the Help Desk ticketing system Inventory and track equipment including equipment loans Greet Help Desk users courteously and direct them appropriately Deliver hardware and set up computers and other equipment Clean workrooms and equipment closets Troubleshoot classroom technology issues Develop troubleshooting skills by using effective investigative methods and using Help Desk troubleshooting tools Requirements: Must have excellent communication skills Must have 2.0 or higher GPA Must be in good judicial standing Preferred: Able to lift 35 lbs Other expectations: Attend monthly meetings/training (approx. 30 min-1 hr) Two original forms of identification needed to complete HR paperwork i.e. passport or driver's license and birth certificate/social security card Additional Information: Wages: $16.00/ hour Application Instructions: Fill out an application.  Be sure to save it to your computer using \"save as\". Upload your application when prompted **Please be sure your Adobe Acrobat software is up to date and that you are opening the application in Internet Explorer. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203424": {
      "title": "Economics",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Economics SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Economics Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Economics Category: Adjunct Instructor Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Aug 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 203424 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is leading the way with cutting-edge programs, including Applied Technology (Architecture, Mechatronics, Construction trades, etc.), Veterinary Science, Nursing, Sustainability, Culinary Arts, Liberal Arts, NCAA Division III athletics, etc.  We are fueled by our passion to become a leader in the higher education space by our commitment to excellence, celebrating diversity, and including faculty, staff and students from all walks of life!  Check out our 60+ award-winning Majors/Programs here . While credentials and technical skills are required, SUNY Delhi values those who are committed to continuous learning/growth, work well independently as well as with a team, and are curious, analytical, and problem-solvers.  Being a champion for our approximately 2,600 students and the SUNY Delhi mission is essential! If you share these values, please consider applying to become part of our team! Located in the beautiful Catskill Mountains with breathtaking views, you may find more information about Delhi, New York, and the surrounding area here. The College offers an outdoor education center, state-of-the-art fitness center, indoor pool, golf simulator, and an 18-hole golf course!  Find a virtual tour of our campus here . See where we rank on US News . Job Description: SUNY Delhi is currently accepting applications for continuous recruitment for Economic Adjunct Instructors in the School of Nursing, Arts and Sciences . Adjunct Instructor positions are part-time Listings are not current vacancies, they are applicant pools; applicant materials are reviewed on an as-needed basis and applicants are contacted when the college determines there is a need List of programs in School of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences: Applied Communication (BS) Biology (AS) Environmental Studies (AS) General Studies (AA, AS) Humanities and Social Sciences (AA) Sustainability (BS) Teacher Education Transfer (AS) Undeclared: Degree Exploration Program Duties may include: Developing and managing course syllabi while adhering to department and college standards Collaborating with colleagues in course curriculum Delivering learning-centered instruction to undergraduate students Assist in the growth and success of a diverse population of students through careful preparation of course materials, effective teaching methodologies, informed critical feedback on assignments and discussions Develop and adapt curriculum incorporating current technologies into the classroom or on-line learning environment (LMS) Implementing school/campus academic and attendance policies Pursuing knowledge of innovations and changes within subject area and field of practice Ability to work effectively in a diverse community and meet the needs of diverse student populations Requirements: Appropriate college level degree as determined by Dean, commensurate with level of course complexity Preferred Qualifications: Master's or PhD Professional experience License in subject area, where applicable Prior teaching experience Prior teaching at the collegiate level Prior on-line course instruction Additional Information: Graduate level teaching assistants, assistant instructors, research assistants and graduate students are encouraged to apply Click here to learn more about what programs and courses we offer For more SUNY Delhi opportunities check out www.delhi.edu/jobs Application Instructions: Please submit: Letter of interest, addressing qualifications, please include subject areas and a listing of classes that you are willing to and/or have experience teaching Curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three professional references SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer. SUNY Delhi does not discriminate. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Your application will not be accepted if you require sponsorship to work in the United States. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203105": {
      "title": "Nursing Clinical Instructors",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Nursing Clinical Instructors SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Nursing Clinical Instructors Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Nursing Clinical Instructors Category: Adjunct Instructor Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Nursing Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Jul 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 203105 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is leading the way with cutting-edge programs, including Applied Technology (Architecture, Mechatronics, Construction trades, etc.), Veterinary Science, Nursing, Sustainability, Culinary Arts, Liberal Arts, NCAA Division III athletics, etc.  We are fueled by our passion to become a leader in the higher education space by our commitment to excellence, celebrating diversity, and including faculty, staff and students from all walks of life!  Check out our 60+ award-winning Majors/Programs here . While credentials and technical skills are required, SUNY Delhi values those who are committed to continuous learning/growth, work well independently as well as with a team, and are curious, analytical, and problem-solvers.  Being a champion for our approximately 2,600 students and the SUNY Delhi mission is essential! If you share these values, please consider applying to become part of our team! Located in the beautiful Catskill Mountains with breathtaking views, you may find more information about Delhi, New York, and the surrounding area here . The College offers an outdoor education center, state-of-the-art fitness center, indoor pool, golf simulator, and an 18-hole golf course!  Find a virtual tour of our campus here . See where we rank on US News Job Description: SUNY Delhi is seeking dynamic and dedicated Adjunct Instructors to teach clinical courses in our pre-licensure nursing program. Clinical learning opportunities are offered in a variety of healthcare settings in Delaware, Otsego and occasionally in surrounding counties.  Adjunct instructor positions are part-time.  Adjuncts may be eligible for generous healthcare benefits based on teaching load. This is a fantastic opportunity to share your real-world experience in a supportive, student-centered environment, helping future nurses build the confidence, skills, and knowledge they need to succeed in the field.  If you have questions, please email nursing@delhi.edu. School of Nursing Majors Offering Clinical Instruction| Registered Nurse Bachelors: Dual Degree Program Duties may include: Clinical Instruction and evaluation of pre-licensure nursing students Developing and managing course syllabi while adhering to department and college standards Collaborating with colleagues in course curriculum Delivering learning-centered instruction to undergraduate students Assist in the growth and success of a diverse population of students through careful preparation of course materials, effective teaching methodologies, informed critical feedback on assignments and discussions Develop and adapt curriculum incorporating current technologies into the clinical learning environment Implementing school/campus academic and attendance policies Pursuing knowledge of innovations and changes within subject area and field of practice Ability to work effectively in a diverse community and meet the needs of diverse student populations Requirements: MSN or enrolled in MSN Program Unencumbered NYS RN License Recent clinical experience Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching experience Prior teaching at the collegiate level Additional Information: SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. Application Instructions: Please submit: Letter of interest, addressing qualifications, please include subject areas and a listing of classes that you are willing to and/or have experience teaching Curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three professional references SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
