chnology Department as part of the A.A.S. and B.S. degree programs. Teaching responsibilities may include traditional classroom lecture, laboratory instruction that may involve live animal handling and clinical skills (e.g., small animals, farm animals, and rodents), and online coursework. Additional duties may include veterinary care for college and visiting animals, student advisement, curriculum development, student retention and enrollment initiatives, and participation in department and college functions and committee work. This is a full-time tenure track position with an academic year obligation (10 months) beginning September 1, 2026. Requirements: Requirements: Hold a LVT/RVT/CVT credential Must be LVT eligible with the ability to be licensed to practice Veterinary Technology in the State of New York within 6 months of employment Bachelor's Degree required.  Candidate must commit to complete a Master degree program within 5 years of employment Minimum 3 years professional/clinical experience Excellent written and oral communication skills; strong attention to detail; and strong computer skills Enthusiasm and aptitude for teaching undergraduate veterinary technology students and preparing them for VTNE certification and entry into professional practice Preferred Qualifications: ALAT, LAT, or LATG certification in lab animal technology Master's Degree or higher in related field College-level teaching and assessment experience Knowledge and use of learning management systems Knowledge and experience with IACUC and AALAS Knowledge and experience with large animals Additional Information: Salary: $50,063.00* This is a 10-month academic year, tenure track position *Rate is subject to change based on release of new salary schedules Application Instructions: SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character and global citizenship. To apply please attach the following items and provide a short statement in your cover letter on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. Cover letter Resume Contact information for three professional references For full consideration please apply by March 20,2026 and will remain posted until filled. SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer. SUNY Delhi does not discriminate. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Your application will not be accepted if you require sponsorship to work in the United States. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
