    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203947": {
      "title": "Energy/Utilities Manager",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Energy/Utilities Manager SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Energy/Utilities Manager Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Energy/Utilities Manager Category: Staff - UUP Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Capital Construction Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Aug 20, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 351538 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $75,000.00 - $75,000.00 Position ID: 203947 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is leading the way with cutting-edge programs, including Applied Technology (Architecture, Mechatronics, Construction trades, etc.), Veterinary Science, Nursing, Sustainability, Culinary Arts, Liberal Arts, NCAA Division III athletics, etc.  We are fueled by our passion to become a leader in the higher education space by our commitment to excellence, celebrating diversity, and including faculty, staff and students from all walks of life!  Check out our 60+ award-winning Majors/Programs here . While credentials and technical skills are required, SUNY Delhi values those who are committed to continuous learning/growth, work well independently as well as with a team, and are curious, analytical, and problem-solvers.  Being a champion for our approximately 2,600 students and the SUNY Delhi mission is essential! If you share these values, please consider applying to become part of our team! Located in the beautiful Catskill Mountains with breathtaking views, you may find more information about Delhi, New York, and the surrounding area here . The College offers an outdoor education center, state-of-the-art fitness center, indoor pool, golf simulator, and an 18-hole golf course!  Find a virtual tour of our campus here . See where we rank on US News Job Description: The Utilities/Energy Manager plans, directs, and oversees the operation, maintenance, repair, and improvement of campus utility systems and related mechanical and electrical infrastructure. The position ensures safe, reliable, efficient, fiscally responsible, and sustainable utility operations that support campus facilities, residents, and visitors. The position develops and oversees proactive maintenance programs; supports long-term capital planning and equipment replacement; coordinates commissioning and retro-commissioning activities; and manages utility outages, emergency repairs, and routine maintenance. The position also coordinates contractors, consultants, vendors, and campus staff and ensures compliance with applicable safety, environmental, and regulatory requirements. Key Responsibilities Supervise employees and contractors performing utility maintenance, repairs, installations, and inspections; ensure quality and safety. Coordinate maintenance and repairs involving electrical distribution, heating and cooling systems, steam, chilled water, water and wastewater systems, SCADA, PLCs, BMS, and related utility infrastructure. Maintain equipment lifecycle records and support capital planning, equipment replacement, energy efficiency, and sustainability initiatives. Coordinate utility outages, emergency repairs, and complex maintenance activities with campus departments, contractors, vendors, and the Heating Plant. Support planning, design, construction, commissioning, and closeout of capital and facilities projects, including review of contract documents and on-site observation of construction activities. Assist with development of budget and administration of utility-related maintenance and service contracts Maintain required utility, maintenance, and regulatory records and documentation. Promote safe work practices and ensure compliance with applicable federal, state, and campus safety, environmental, hazardous materials, and hazardous waste requirements. Perform hands-on technical work when necessary to support the operation and maintenance of campus utility systems. Requirements: Minimum of six (6) years of experience in construction trades, utility operations, facilities maintenance, or a related field; three (3) years of which in supervisory experience in the field. OR An associate degree in Construction Management, Architecture, Engineering, or a related field and 4 years of experience in construction trades, utility operations, facilities maintenance, or a related field; three (3) years of which in supervisory experience in the field. Experience operating, maintaining, and repairing utility, mechanical, and electrical systems in an institutional, commercial, or campus environment, including electrical distribution, HVAC, steam, chilled water, water distribution, and related CMMS, BMS, or SCADA systems. Working knowledge of industry practices, tools, terminology, and safety standards related to electrical and mechanical trades. Demonstrated management and administrative skills Strong verbal and written communication skills Valid New York State driver's license. Preferred Qualifications Ten (10) years' experience in the operation, maintenance, and management of utility production and distribution systems, associated mechanical and electrical equipment, and Building Management Systems (BMS). Higher Education or public-sector experience in facilities operations or procurement. Familiarity with SUNY procurement systems and procedures. Knowledge of construction-related procurement and contracting. Experience with energy management, energy efficiency, or sustainability initiatives. Additional Information: Starting date: As soon as possible Work schedule: Monday through Friday Salary:  Starting at $75,000, or commensurate with experience Reports to: Associate Vice President of Operations Budget Title:  Senior Staff Assistant, SL3 This position offers full New York State UUP (FT) benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country with an excellent fringe benefits package Click here for more Information for Prospective Employees SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. If you need a disability-related accommodation, please contact nochevgn@delhi.edu Clery Statement Applicants interested in positions may access the Annual Security Report (ASR) for SUNY Delhi online. The ASR contains information on campus security policies and certain campus crime statistics. Crime statistics are reported in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Applicants may request a hard copy of the ASR by contacting the SUNY Delhi University Police Department at 607-746-4700. Application Instructions: To apply, please submit: Letter of interest Resume or Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three professional references Optional statement requested: SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity, and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character, and global citizenship. Please provide a short statement on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. For full consideration, please apply by September 20. 2026. The position will remain open until filled. SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer. SUNY Delhi does not discriminate. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Your application will not be accepted if you require sponsorship to work in the United States. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
