    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203070": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Care Coordination & Well-Being",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Care Coordination & Well-Being SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Care Coordination & Well-Being Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Care Coordination & Well-Being Category: Staff - UUP Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Rights and Responsibilities Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Aug 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 352049 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $58,000.00 - $58,000.00 Position ID: 203070 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is leading the way with cutting-edge programs, including Applied Technology (Architecture, Mechatronics, Construction trades, etc.), Veterinary Science, Nursing, Sustainability, Culinary Arts, Liberal Arts, NCAA Division III athletics, etc. We are fueled by our passion to become a leader in the higher education space by our commitment to excellence, celebrating diversity, and including faculty, staff and students from all walks of life! Check out our 60+ award-winning Majors/Programs here https://www.delhi.edu/academics/majors-programs/index.php . While credentials and technical skills are required, SUNY Delhi values those who are committed to continuous learning/growth, work well independently as well as with a team, and are curious, analytical, and problem-solvers. Being a champion for our approximately 2,600 students and the SUNY Delhi mission https://www.delhi.edu/about/president-office/strategic-plan/index.php is essential! If you share these values, please consider applying to become part of our team! Located in the beautiful Catskill Mountains with breathtaking views, you may find more information about Delhi, New York, and the surrounding area here https://www.visitdelhiny.com/ . The College offers an outdoor education center, state-of-the-art fitness center, indoor pool, golf simulator, and an 18-hole golf course! Find a virtual tour of our campus here https://www.delhi.edu/admission/visit-delhi/index.php . See where we rank on US News https://www.usnews.com/best-colleges/suny-college-of-technology-delhi-2857 Job Description: The Assistant Director of Care Coordination and Well-Being combines student case management (40-50%), behavioral health and suicide prevention programming, campus training and outreach, CARE Team coordination, and cross-campus/community partnership development to support student well-being, retention, and success. Key Duties Serve as the primary non-clinical case manager for students experiencing personal, behavioral health, mental health, substance use, or other challenges affecting academic success and well-being. Coordinate with the CARE Team and campus partners to connect students with campus and community resources and provide ongoing support during crises, hospitalization, medical leave, treatment, and return-to-campus transitions. Collaborate with Counseling & Health Services to develop and implement prevention and wellness programs focused on: Suicide prevention Substance use prevention Mental health awareness Resilience and stress management Healthy relationships and conflict resolution Overall student well-being Partner with Counseling and Health Services to coordinate campus-wide training and education initiatives, including programs such as QPR and Mental Health First Aid. Lead campus mediation and conflict resolution services. Support behavioral intervention and threat assessment processes. Collect, analyze, and report data related to case management services, student outcomes, and prevention programming. Build and maintain partnerships with campus departments and community organizations to strengthen support networks and referral resources. Conduct outreach, presentations, workshops, and awareness campaigns promoting help-seeking behaviors and student wellness. Provide consultation and guidance to faculty, staff, and others supporting students of concern. Requirements: Bachelor's Degree Two or more years of experience in Human Services, Education or Community Initiatives Demonstrated cultural competency and cultural humility, including the ability to build trust and rapport with students across race, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, socioeconomic status, disability, religion, national origin, and other dimensions of identity. Demonstrated experience working effectively with diverse student populations and historically marginalized or underrepresented communities. Commitment to equity-minded, inclusive, and identity-conscious practice in case management, prevention, and crisis response. Preferred Experience MSW or related degree Behavioral intervention, case management, or crisis response Suicide prevention, mental health, and substance misuse prevention Conflict resolution, motivational interviewing, and trauma-informed practices Culturally responsive programming and supporting diverse student populations Additional Information: Starting: October 2026 Work schedule: 11-month, college-year; month of Non-obligation: July Starting Salary: $58,000 Reports to: Director of Community Standards and Well-Being Budget Title:  Senior Staff Assistant, SL3 This position offers full New York State UUP (FT) benefits, which are among the most comprehensive in the country with an excellent fringe benefits package Click here for more Information for Prospective Employees SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. If you need a disability-related accommodation, please contact nochevgn@delhi.edu Clery Statement Applicants interested in positions may access the Annual Security Report (ASR) for SUNY Delhi online. The ASR contains information on campus security policies and certain campus crime statistics. Crime statistics are reported in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Applicants may request a hard copy of the ASR by contacting the SUNY Delhi University Police Department at 607-746-4700. Application Instructions: To apply, please attach the following items and provide a short statement in your cover letter on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. Cover letter Resume Contact information for three professional references For full consideration, please apply by September 7, 2026 ; the position will remain posted until filled. SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character and global citizenship. SUNY Delhi is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran status, disability or membership in any other class protected by Federal, State, or local law. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202932": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Project Coordinator SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Project Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Project Coordinator Category: Staff - UUP Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Capital Construction Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Jul 27, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 350123 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $57,151.00 - $57,151.00 Position ID: 202932 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is leading the way with cutting-edge programs, including Applied Technology (Architecture, Mechatronics, Construction trades, etc.), Veterinary Science, Nursing, Sustainability, Culinary Arts, Liberal Arts, NCAA Division III athletics, etc.  We are fueled by our passion to become a leader in the higher education space by our commitment to excellence, celebrating diversity, and including faculty, staff and students from all walks of life!  Check out our 60+ award-winning Majors/Programs here . While credentials and technical skills are required, SUNY Delhi values those who are committed to continuous learning/growth, work well independently as well as with a team, and are curious, analytical, and problem-solvers.  Being a champion for our approximately 2,600 students and the SUNY Delhi mission is essential! If you share these values, please consider applying to become part of our team! Located in the beautiful Catskill Mountains with breathtaking views, you may find more information about Delhi, New York, and the surrounding area here . The College offers an outdoor education center, state-of-the-art fitness center, indoor pool, golf simulator, and an 18-hole golf course!  Find a virtual tour of our campus here . See where we rank on US News Job Description: The Project Coordinator supports the planning, coordination, and execution of capital construction, renovation, and infrastructure projects across campus. This role assists Project Managers and campus leadership in ensuring projects are completed on time, within scope, and in compliance with SUNY policies, New York State regulations, and applicable codes. Key Responsibilities Assist in the coordination of capital projects from initiation through closeout.  This includes planning, design, construction, turnover and post project support. Track project schedules, budgets, and deliverables; provide regular status updates and generate any reports as needed Coordinate communication between internal campus departments, SUCF, consultants, contractors, and vendors Prepare and maintain project documentation, including contracts, change orders, and reports Properly file all associated project documentation Support and assist in associated project procurements in accordance with SUNY Delhi and New York State guidelines Monitor project compliance with applicable codes, safety standards, and campus policies Assist with site visits, inspections, and project meetings Directly oversee all aspects of construction of capital projects on campus to ensure contractor(s) are following contract documents Responsible for safety and overall capital construction sites on campus Review invoices and assist with payment processing and budget tracking for capital projects Maintain accurate project records and filing system Provide administrative and logistical support for the capital department Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Associate's degree in Construction Management, Engineering, Architecture, Business Administration, or a related field Requirements: 1-3  years of experience in project coordination, construction, facilities, or a related area Strong organizational and time management skills Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, Outlook) Ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines Preferred Qualifications: Associate's degree in Construction Management, Engineering, Architecture, Business Administration, or a related field 3-5 years of experience in project coordination, construction, facilities, or a related area Experience working in higher education, public sector, or unionized environments Familiarity with New York State procurement and contracting procedures Knowledge of construction processes, drawings, and project lifecycle Experience with project management software (e.g., Procore, Primavera, or similar) Understanding of applicable building codes and safety regulations Additional Information: Starting date: As soon as possible Work schedule: Monday through Friday Salary:  Starting at $57,151, commensurate with experience Reports to: Assistant Director of Capital Construction Budget Title:  Senior Staff Assistant, SL3 This position offers full New York State UUP (FT) benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country with an excellent fringe benefits package Click here for more Information for Prospective Employees SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. If you need a disability-related accommodation, please contact nochevgn@delhi.edu Clery Statement Applicants interested in positions may access the Annual Security Report (ASR) for SUNY Delhi online. The ASR contains information on campus security policies and certain campus crime statistics. Crime statistics are reported in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Applicants may request a hard copy of the ASR by contacting the SUNY Delhi University Police Department at 607-746-4700. Application Instructions: To apply, please submit: Letter of interest Resume or Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three professional references Optional statement requested: SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity, and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character, and global citizenship. Please provide a short statement on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. For full consideration, please apply by August 29, 2026. Position will remain open until filled. SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer. SUNY Delhi does not discriminate. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Your application will not be accepted if you require sponsorship to work in the United States. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203447": {
      "title": "University Police Communications & Security Specialist 1 - NY HELPS",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: University Police Communications & Security Specialist 1 - NY HELPS SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: University Police Communications & Security Specialist 1 - NY HELPS Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details University Police Communications & Security Specialist 1 - NY HELPS Category: University Police Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: University Police Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Aug 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $49,454.00 - $49,454.00 Position ID: 203447 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is leading the way with cutting-edge programs, including Applied Technology (Architecture, Mechatronics, Construction trades, etc.), Veterinary Science, Nursing, Sustainability, Culinary Arts, Liberal Arts, NCAA Division III athletics, etc.  We are fueled by our passion to become a leader in the higher education space by our commitment to excellence, celebrating diversity, and including faculty, staff and students from all walks of life!  Check out our 60+ award-winning Majors/Programs here . While credentials and technical skills are required, SUNY Delhi values those who are committed to continuous learning/growth, work well independently as well as with a team, and are curious, analytical, and problem-solvers.  Being a champion for our approximately 2,600 students and the SUNY Delhi mission is essential! If you share these values, please consider applying to become part of our team! Located in the beautiful Catskill Mountains with breathtaking views, you may find more information about Delhi, New York, and the surrounding area here. The College offers an outdoor education center, state-of-the-art fitness center, indoor pool, golf simulator, and an 18-hole golf course!  Find a virtual tour of our campus here . See where we rank on US News . Job Description: SUNY Delhi seeks a dynamic and engaging University Police Communications & Security Specialist to work as part of the University Police team. SUNY Delhi prides itself on being a welcoming college community for all. Diversity, equity, and inclusiveness are integral components of the highest quality academic programs and the strongest campus climate. The college seeks a wide range of applicants for its positions so that inclusive excellence will be affirmed. University Police Communications and Security Specialists provide communications, security, and public safety services within a 24/7 operation in the University Police Department on the SUNY Delhi campus. The primary responsibilities are to function as the initial point of contact between the police and the public, perform dispatching activities, and use various databases, online systems, and multiple video sources. They have neither peace nor police officer status. University Police Communications and Security Specialist 1 function under the direction of the University Police Department shift supervisor, typically a University Police Officer 2. Incumbents are given directions regarding assignments, briefing on current problems at the beginning of the shift, and instruction in job-related law enforcement techniques. Requirements: The successful candidate must: Be reachable for appointment on a present, permanent Civil Service eligible list for University Police Communications & Security Specialist I, or NY HELPS Have previously held the University Police Communications & Security Specialist I Title. If appointed to this position, candidates must obtain a Security Guard Photo ID from the NYS Dept of State within 90 days of appointment, which requires an 8-hour pre-assignment course. Note: If you are not active on the Civil Service list and have not taken the test, you must meet the minimum qualifications to sit for the exam. Exam requirements are: Either 1. one year of full time experience as a Police or Peace Officer; Or 2. one year of full time experience as a dispatcher for a public safety agency including fire departments, emergency medical services, or law enforcement; Or 3. one year of active service and an Honorable Discharge from the United States military, where you served as a dispatcher or military police/security personnel; Or 4. 30 semester college credit hours from an accredited school (see note #1). NY HELPS Summary: *For the duration of the NY HELPS Program, this title maybe filled via a non - competitive appointment, which means no examination is required but all candidates must meet the minimum qualifications of the title for which they apply. At this time, agencies may recruit and hire employees by making temporary appointments. In May 2024, if a temporary NY HELPS employee is satisfactorily performing in the position, the appointment will be changed from temporary pending Civil Service Commission Action to permanent non-competitive and the official probationary period will begin. At a future date (within one year of permanent appointment), it is expected employees hired under NY HELPS will have their non-competitive employment status converted to competitive status, without having to compete in an examination. Employees will then be afforded with all of the same rights and privileges of competitive class employees of New York State. While serving permanently in a NY HELPS title, employees may take part in any promotion examination for which they are qualified. The NY HELPS program for the state workforce expires on June 30, 2028. Additional Information: Appointment: Full-time, Contingent Permanent Negotiation Unit: 21 - NYSCOPA, Salary Grade: 10 Starting Salary: $49,454 Schedule: 12 hr shifts,  7 to 7, days off rotate weekly, but are fixed. Location: University Police Department, SUNY Delhi This position offers full New York State NYSCOPBA benefits , which are among the most comprehensive in the country. SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct criminal background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. Application Instructions: To apply, please submit: Letter of interest Resume Contact information for three professional references Full consideration for this September 6, 2026 Position will remain posted until filled SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer. SUNY Delhi does not discriminate. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Your application will not be accepted if you require sponsorship to work in the United States. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203483": {
      "title": "Shuttle Driver (Fall 2026)",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Shuttle Driver (Fall 2026) SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Shuttle Driver (Fall 2026) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Shuttle Driver (Fall 2026) Category: Active Student Jobs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Transportation Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Aug 11, 2026 Closes: Dec 31, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Part-time Ref. No.: RTF #353051 Position ID: 203483 Share Job Description: SUNY Delhi is seeking a courteous, reliable, and efficient student with driving experience to provide transportation between the SUNY Delhi Main Campus and several local destinations, including Riverview Townhouses, Price Chopper, O'Connor Hospital, Valley Campus, and the Village of Delhi. Duties Include: Transporting students between the Main Campus and local stops, including Riverview Townhouses, Valley Campus, Bluestone Restaurant, Price Chopper Plaza, and the Village of Delhi on an 'will-call' basis. Students will contact the Shuttle Driver directly for rides. Assisting students with relocating between residence halls from the Main Campus to Riverview Townhouses. Requests will be made directly by Residence Life staff and may include helping with moving student belongings. Serving as a substitute driver when the scheduled Shuttle Driver is unavailable. Requirements: Ability to perform duties typically associated with driving a motor vehicle. Maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.30. Be in good judicial standing with the College. Possess a valid NYS Driver's License with driving experience and no moving violations. Work efficiently with minimal supervision. Additional Information: Shuttle Schedule: Monday - Friday: 6 pm - 10 pm Saturday and Sunday: 3 pm - 10 pm Additional Information: Students must pick up the keys to the Shuttle 15 minutes before the start of their shift at the University Police Department in North Hall. Application Instructions: Fill out an Application.  (Be sure to save it to your computer using \"save as\") Upload your application AND resume when prompted **Please be sure your Adobe Acrobat software is up to date and that you are opening the application in Internet Explorer. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    }
